<title>INDIA: India HDFC Bank 96/97 net doubles.</title>
<headline>India HDFC Bank 96/97 net doubles.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	   (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  405.0   vs	 202.8</p>
<p>    Interest income	 1,617.4   vs     1,145.6</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	     0.8   vs	  Nil</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	     2.03  vs	  ---</p>
<p>    Other income		315.9   vs	 135.3</p>
<p>    Interest expenses	 871.8   vs	 708.4</p>
<p>    Other expenditure	 418.4   vs	 274.5</p>
<p>    Gross profit		643.1   vs	 298.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation		 62.8   vs	  15.8</p>
<p>    Tax			   175.3   vs	  79.4</p>
<p>Note - HDFC Bank Ltd is promoted by Housing Development Finance Corporation Ltd. It has a strategic alliance with NatWest Markets, the investment banking arm of Britain's National Westminster Bank Plc. The NatWest group holds 20 percent of HDFC Bank's equity.</p>
<p>The bank said other income comprises commissions, fees and foreign exchange earnings.</p>
<p>Deposits rose 87 percent and loan advances grew 56 percent, it said in a statement without giving details.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
